---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Physics Module 4 Test">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="header">
			<p class="eyebrow">Exploring Creation with Physics</p>
			<h1>Physics Module 4 Test</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">Motion in Two Dimensions</p>
		</div>

		<form id="module4Test" autocomplete="off">
			<div class="card">
				<h2>Student Information</h2>
				<div class="form-row">
					<label>
						Full Name
						<input type="text" id="studentName" required>
					</label>
					<label>
						Email Address
						<input type="email" id="studentEmail" required>
					</label>
				</div>
				<input type="text" id="website" style="display: none;" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
			</div>

			<div class="card captcha-card">
				<label>
					Security Check: What is <span id="captcha-question"></span>?
					<input type="number" id="captcha" required>
				</label>
				<div id="captcha-error" style="display: none;">Incorrect answer. Please try again.</div>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 1</h3>
				<p>A projectile launched from level ground hits a target on the ground several meters away from the launch site. If the projectile hits the target with a speed of 124 m/sec, what was the initial speed with which the projectile was fired?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q1" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 2</h3>
				<p>A bullet is fired at a target which is at the same height as the gun from which the bullet was fired. If the bullet takes 0.44 seconds to hit the target, how long did it take for the bullet to reach its maximum height?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q2" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 3</h3>
				<p>A military rocket is equipped with thruster engines that allow it to navigate towards its target. These thrusters fight gravity so that the vertical acceleration the projectile experiences is greatly reduced. In addition, the thrusters allow the rocket to accelerate horizontally. Do you expect this rocket to travel on a parabolic path? Why or why not?</p>
				<textarea id="q3" class="answer-input" rows="3" required></textarea>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 4</h3>
				<p>What one condition must apply before you can use the range equation [Equation (4.9)]?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q4" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 5</h3>
				<p>If you double the initial speed of a projectile, what happens to that projectile's range? Assume that the projectile lands at the height from which it was launched.</p>
				<input type="text" id="q5" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 6</h3>
				<p>Suppose you used Equation (4.9) to calculate the range of a projectile. If you were to make another calculation in which you included the effect of air resistance, would the calculated range increase or decrease? Assume that the projectile lands at the height from which it was launched.</p>
				<input type="text" id="q6" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 7</h3>
				<p>The y-component of a projectile's velocity is 12.1 m/sec. When the projectile once again passes by the height from which it was launched, what is the y-component of its velocity?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q7" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 8</h3>
				<p>Which of the following objects would move in a parabolic path?</p>
				<div class="radio-group">
					<label class="radio-option">
						<input type="radio" name="q8" value="a" required>
						a. A rock thrown with an angle of 40&deg; relative to the ground
					</label>
					<label class="radio-option">
						<input type="radio" name="q8" value="b" required>
						b. A jet airplane using its engines in flight
					</label>
					<label class="radio-option">
						<input type="radio" name="q8" value="c" required>
						c. A rocket in space
					</label>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 9</h3>
				<p>A projectile is fired with a certain initial velocity from the surface of the earth. If the same projectile were taken to the moon and shot from the surface of the moon with the same initial velocity, would it have a larger, smaller, or identical range? Why? Assume that the projectile lands at the height from which it was launched.</p>
				<textarea id="q9" class="answer-input" rows="3" required></textarea>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 10</h3>
				<p>An explorer follows these directions:</p>
				<p class="question-detail">Travel with a constant velocity of 2.1 m/sec at a heading of 120.0 degrees for 1.1 hours, then turn to a heading of 200.0 degrees and travel at the same speed for 2.3 hours.</p>
				<p>What will the explorer's final displacement be? (Include magnitude and direction; show your work.)</p>
				<textarea id="q10" class="answer-input" rows="3" required></textarea>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 11</h3>
				<p>An archer lies on the ground and lets loose an arrow with an initial velocity of 112 ft/sec at &theta; = 40.0&deg;. What is the maximum height that the arrow will reach?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q11" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 12</h3>
				<p>What is the range of a gun that fires its bullets with a velocity of 175 m/sec at an angle of 30.0 degrees? Assume the bullets land at the height from which they were launched.</p>
				<input type="text" id="q12" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 13</h3>
				<p>Aimed at an angle of 45 degrees, a cannon has a range of 4,123 feet. What is the initial speed of a cannonball launched from this cannon? Assume the cannonballs land at the height from which they were launched.</p>
				<input type="text" id="q13" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 14</h3>
				<p>A diver is on a hill overlooking a lake. If the hill is 45 feet above the surface of the water and the diver jumps horizontally (&theta; = 0&deg;) with an initial speed of 20.0 ft/sec, how far from the hill will the diver hit the lake?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q14" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<h3>Question 15</h3>
				<p>In an archery competition, an archer stands on a hill so that the arrow in her bow is 20.0 meters above the ground and is aimed at an angle of 0&deg; relative to the ground. If the archer is trying to hit a target that lies on the ground 118 m away, with what initial velocity must she launch her arrow?</p>
				<input type="text" id="q15" class="answer-input" required>
			</div>

			<button type="submit" class="submit-button">Submit Test</button>
		</form>

		<div id="results" style="display: none;" class="card">
			<h2>Test Submitted</h2>
			<p id="email-status">Your answers have been sent to your instructor.</p>
			<button type="button" class="submit-button" onclick="window.location.reload()">Take Again</button>
		</div>
	</div>

	<script type="text/javascript" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@emailjs/browser@3/dist/email.min.js" is:inline></script>

	<script is:inline>
		let captchaAnswer = 0;

		function generateCaptcha() {
			const num1 = Math.floor(Math.random() * 10) + 1;
			const num2 = Math.floor(Math.random() * 10) + 1;
			captchaAnswer = num1 + num2;
			document.getElementById('captcha-question').textContent = `${num1} + ${num2}`;
		}

		function validateCaptcha() {
			const userAnswer = parseInt(document.getElementById('captcha').value);
			const errorDiv = document.getElementById('captcha-error');
			if (userAnswer !== captchaAnswer) {
				errorDiv.style.display = 'block';
				generateCaptcha();
				document.getElementById('captcha').value = '';
				return false;
			}
			errorDiv.style.display = 'none';
			return true;
		}

		function validateSecurity() {
			const honeypot = document.getElementById('website');
			if (honeypot && honeypot.value) {
				console.log('Spam bot detected via honeypot');
				alert('Security check failed. Please try again.');
				return false;
			}

			const lastSubmission = localStorage.getItem('lastQuizStart');
			const now = Date.now();
			if (lastSubmission && (now - parseInt(lastSubmission)) < 30000) {
				alert('Please wait 30 seconds between attempts.');
				return false;
			}
			localStorage.setItem('lastQuizStart', now.toString());

			if (!validateCaptcha()) {
				return false;
			}

			const email = document.getElementById('studentEmail').value;
			const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
			if (!emailRegex.test(email)) {
				alert('Please enter a valid email address.');
				return false;
			}

			const spamDomains = ['tempmail.org', '10minutemail.com', 'guerrillamail.com', 'mailinator.com', 'throwaway.email'];
			const domain = email.split('@')[1].toLowerCase();
			if (spamDomains.includes(domain)) {
				alert('Please use a permanent email address.');
				return false;
			}

			return true;
		}

		window.onload = function() {
			try {
				emailjs.init('ct_s19oZHppLy9BlW');
			} catch (e) {
				console.error('EmailJS init failed:', e);
			}
			generateCaptcha();
		};

		document.getElementById('module4Test').addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
			e.preventDefault();

			if (!validateSecurity()) {
				return;
			}

			const studentName = document.getElementById('studentName').value.trim();
			const studentEmail = document.getElementById('studentEmail').value.trim();
			const now = new Date().toLocaleString();

			const q8choice = document.querySelector('input[name="q8"]:checked');
			const q8letter = q8choice ? q8choice.value : '';
			const q8text = { a: 'a. A rock thrown with an angle of 40 degrees relative to the ground', b: 'b. A jet airplane using its engines in flight', c: 'c. A rocket in space' }[q8letter] || '';

			const answers = [
				['Question 1', document.getElementById('q1').value.trim()],
				['Question 2', document.getElementById('q2').value.trim()],
				['Question 3', document.getElementById('q3').value.trim()],
				['Question 4', document.getElementById('q4').value.trim()],
				['Question 5', document.getElementById('q5').value.trim()],
				['Question 6', document.getElementById('q6').value.trim()],
				['Question 7', document.getElementById('q7').value.trim()],
				['Question 8', q8text],
				['Question 9', document.getElementById('q9').value.trim()],
				['Question 10', document.getElementById('q10').value.trim()],
				['Question 11', document.getElementById('q11').value.trim()],
				['Question 12', document.getElementById('q12').value.trim()],
				['Question 13', document.getElementById('q13').value.trim()],
				['Question 14', document.getElementById('q14').value.trim()],
				['Question 15', document.getElementById('q15').value.trim()]
			];

			let message = `PHYSICS MODULE 4 TEST SUBMISSION\n`;
			message += `Submitted: ${now}\n\n`;
			message += `Student: ${studentName}\n`;
			message += `Student Email: ${studentEmail}\n\n`;
			message += `ANSWERS:\n`;
			answers.forEach((item) => {
				message += `\n${item[0]}\n   ${item[1]}\n`;
			});

			const templateParams = {
				to_email: 'chuck@c00lnerd.com',
				from_name: 'C00lnerd Quiz System',
				from_email: 'chuck@c00lnerd.com',
				message: message,
				subject: `Physics Module 4 Test - ${studentName}`
			};

			window.emailjs.send('service_kaw1xkh', 'template_io02xtm', templateParams)
				.then(function(response) {
					console.log('Email sent:', response.status, response.text);
					document.getElementById('module4Test').style.display = 'none';
					document.getElementById('results').style.display = 'block';
					document.getElementById('email-status').textContent = 'Your test has been submitted and emailed to your instructor.';
				}, function(error) {
					console.error('Email error:', error);
					if (error && error.text) console.error('Error details:', error.text);
					alert('There was an error sending your test. Please check your internet connection and try again.');
				});
		});
	</script>

	<style>
		.container {
			max-width: 800px;
			margin: 0 auto;
			padding: 2rem 1rem;
			font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
		}

		.header {
			text-align: center;
			margin-bottom: 2rem;
		}

		.eyebrow {
			text-transform: uppercase;
			letter-spacing: 0.08em;
			font-weight: 700;
			color: #2563eb;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
		}

		h1 {
			margin: 0;
			font-size: 2.2rem;
			color: #111827;
		}

		.subtitle {
			color: #4b5563;
			font-size: 1.1rem;
			margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
		}

		.card {
			background: white;
			border-radius: 12px;
			box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
			padding: 1.5rem;
			margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
		}

		.card h2,
		.card h3 {
			margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
			color: #111827;
		}

		.card p {
			color: #374151;
			line-height: 1.6;
			margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
		}

		.question-detail {
			font-style: italic;
			padding-left: 1rem;
			border-left: 3px solid #d1d5db;
		}

		.radio-group {
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 0.5rem;
		}

		.radio-option {
			display: flex;
			align-items: flex-start;
			gap: 0.5rem;
			font-weight: 400;
			color: #374151;
			line-height: 1.5;
		}

		.radio-option input[type="radio"] {
			margin-top: 0.3rem;
		}

		.form-row {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1rem;
		}

		@media (min-width: 600px) {
			.form-row {
				grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
			}
		}

		label {
			display: block;
			font-weight: 600;
			color: #374151;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
		}

		input[type="text"],
		input[type="email"],
		input[type="number"],
		textarea,
		.answer-input {
			width: 100%;
			padding: 0.75rem;
			margin-top: 0.35rem;
			border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
			border-radius: 6px;
			font-size: 1rem;
			box-sizing: border-box;
			font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
		}

		.answer-input {
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.captcha-card label {
			display: block;
		}

		#captcha-error {
			color: #dc2626;
			margin-top: 0.5rem;
			font-weight: 600;
		}

		.submit-button {
			display: inline-block;
			width: 100%;
			padding: 1rem;
			font-size: 1.1rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			color: white;
			background: #2563eb;
			border: none;
			border-radius: 8px;
			cursor: pointer;
			margin-top: 1rem;
		}

		.submit-button:hover {
			background: #1d4ed8;
		}

		#results {
			text-align: center;
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
